issue.body:
Hello,

This message was written with the help of AI to solve an issue while booting Supernova with lots of UGen extensions and where the booting time was insanely slow. With different adjustments, I succeeded to boot Supernova almost in the same way as scsynth apparently on my Mac. I will share several improvements I found with the AI to speed up Supernova on Mac. I tried to split them as much as possible. Here is the second one. I do not know if it is the best way. But with this fix, the speed up of booting is really quick.

## Environment

* SuperCollider version: Latest Dev.
* Operating system: macOS 27, Apple M1 Max
* Other details (Qt version, audio driver, etc.): supernova server

## Summary

Plugins ship as pairs, one build per server, in the same folder (`BinaryOpUGens.scx` and `BinaryOpUGens_supernova.scx`). 
At boot, supernova fully opens the scsynth build of every pair, only to close it again. 
The proposed fix skips a scsynth build without opening it when its `_supernova` version is in the same folder to speed up dramatically the boot process of Supernova on Mac at least.

## Steps to reproduce

Run this in the IDE. It starts supernova with the core plugins only, for 3 seconds, and lists the scsynth builds it opens:

```supercollider
(
// Lists the scsynth builds that supernova opens at boot (core plugins only).
var dir = Platform.resourceDir.shellQuote;
var cmd = "cd % && (DYLD_PRINT_LIBRARIES=1 ./supernova -u 57999 -U plugins & p=$!; sleep 3; kill $p) 2>&1"
    " | grep -o '[^/]*\\.scx$' | grep -v '_supernova\\.scx$'";
var opened = cmd.format(dir).unixCmdGetStdOut.split($\n).reject(_.isEmpty);
"scsynth builds opened by supernova: %".format(opened.size).postln;
opened.do { |name| ("  " ++ name).postln };
)
```

## Expected vs. actual behavior

**Expected:** supernova opens only the scsynth builds that have no supernova version. Among the core plugins, that is `Link_UGen.scx` alone.

**Actual (develop):** it opens all 27 core scsynth builds:

```
scsynth builds opened by supernova: 27
  UIUGens.scx
  GrainUGens.scx
  PanUGens.scx
  ...
  Link_UGen.scx
  ...
  ReverbUGens.scx
```

**With the fix:**

```
scsynth builds opened by supernova: 1
  Link_UGen.scx
```

## Problem

**File:** `server/supernova/sc/sc_ugen_factory.cpp`

`load_plugin_folder()` (line 216) calls `load_plugin()` on every `.scx` file (line 236). `load_plugin()` (line 313) opens the file with `dlopen(..., RTLD_NOW | RTLD_LOCAL)`, and only afterwards checks which server it was built for (line 327):

```cpp
info_function supernova_check = reinterpret_cast<info_function>(dlsym(handle, "server_type"));
if (!supernova_check || (*supernova_check)() == sc_server_scsynth) {
    // silently ignore
    dlclose(handle);
    return;
}
```

So every scsynth build is loaded, has all its symbols bound and its static initializers run, and is then closed without being used.

## Possible Fix

**File to modify:** `server/supernova/sc/sc_ugen_factory.cpp`, 3 places (line numbers from develop 5d47207bb).

**1. Before line 216** (just before `load_plugin_folder()`): add a helper that recognizes a scsynth build (`Foo.scx` or `Foo_scsynth.scx`) whose `Foo_supernova.scx` is in the same folder.

```diff
@@ -213,6 +213,30 @@
     return true;
 }

+namespace {
+
+bool ends_with(std::string const& s, std::string const& suffix) {
+    return s.size() >= suffix.size() && s.compare(s.size() - suffix.size(), suffix.size(), suffix) == 0;
+}
+
+// "Foo.scx" or "Foo_scsynth.scx" next to "Foo_supernova.scx" is the scsynth build: load_plugin would
+// dlopen it only to reject it.
+bool is_scsynth_twin_of_supernova_plugin(std::filesystem::path const& file) {
+    static const std::string supernova_suffix = "_supernova";
+    static const std::string scsynth_suffix = "_scsynth";
+    std::string base = file.stem().string();
+    if (ends_with(base, supernova_suffix))
+        return false;
+    if (ends_with(base, scsynth_suffix))
+        base.erase(base.size() - scsynth_suffix.size());
+
+    std::error_code ec;
+    return std::filesystem::exists(file.parent_path() / (base + supernova_suffix + SC_PLUGIN_EXT), ec);
+}
+
+} // namespace
+
 void sc_ugen_factory::load_plugin_folder(std::filesystem::path const& dir) {
```

**2. Line 235**, in `load_plugin_folder()`: skip those files.

```diff
@@ -232,7 +256,7 @@
     for (const auto& entry : iter) {
         if (fs::is_regular_file(entry.status())) {
             // Ignore files that don't have the extension of an SC plugin
-            if (entry.path().extension() == SC_PLUGIN_EXT) {
+            if (entry.path().extension() == SC_PLUGIN_EXT && !is_scsynth_twin_of_supernova_plugin(entry.path())) {
                 load_plugin(entry.path());
             }
```

**3. Line 265**, same change in the `LINUX_PLUGIN_WORKAROUND` variant of `load_plugin_folder()`.

```diff
@@ -262,7 +286,8 @@
     for (const auto& entry : fs::directory_iterator(dir, options)) {
         if (fs::is_regular_file(entry.status()) && entry.path().extension() == SC_PLUGIN_EXT) {
-            load_plugin(entry.path());
+            if (!is_scsynth_twin_of_supernova_plugin(entry.path()))
+                load_plugin(entry.path());
             found_scx_file = true;
         }
```

`found_scx_file = true` stays unconditional, so the `.so` handling of that variant does not change.

## What the fix changes

* **Faster boot.** supernova no longer opens the scsynth half of each plugin pair. Among the core plugins, 26 of the 27 `dlopen` calls on scsynth builds disappear. Every third-party plugin package that ships both builds (sc3-plugins, for example) adds more pairs, so the gain grows with the number of installed plugins.
* **Same UGens available.** Every `_supernova` plugin is still loaded, and the scsynth builds that were skipped would have been rejected anyway.
* **No change for plugins without a supernova version.** They are still opened and checked exactly as before (`Link_UGen.scx` above).
* **No change for scsynth.** The fix only touches supernova's plugin loader.

Related: #7731 (the other cause of slow supernova boot on macOS).
```
